config AIRPLAY_ENABLE
    bool "Enable AirPlay (RAOP) receiver"
    default n
    help
        Vendors an AirPlay 1 (RAOP) receiver (esp-raop-receiver, from
        codeberg.org/Edu_Coder/esp-airsync - see modules/airplay/UPSTREAM.md)
        plus Apple's own open-source ALAC decoder, in place of upstream's
        prebuilt libalac.a. Wired into main/app_main.cpp (a non-fatal
        airplay_init() call, same pattern as audio_init()), feeds decoded
        PCM into modules/audio's streaming sink for the session's lifetime,
        registers its own tray indicator, and disables Wi-Fi power save
        while a session is open. Defaults off, and unlike audio's "cheap
        and harmless when idle" default-on, this has real costs even before
        anyone streams to it:

        - The RSA key AirPlay 1's handshake needs (Apple's AirPort Express
          private key) is not shipped in this repository and never will be
          - turning this on without supplying your own copy at
          modules/airplay/secrets/raop_private_key.pem (gitignored) fails
          the build with an explanatory message. See README.md, "The RSA
          key situation".
        - AirPlay needs Wi-Fi power save disabled and sustained CPU for the
          RTSP/RTP/ALAC/mDNS work, which this board's battery-drain
          tracking makes a real, measured cost, not a hypothetical one -
          see README.md, "Power".
        - Roughly 86KiB of flash and, once a client actually connects,
          about 1.3MB of PSRAM for the RTP jitter buffer and decoded-PCM
          ring (see README.md, "Buffer sizing" and "What is unverified").

        Turning this on proves the receiver, ALAC decoder, and the wiring
        into modules/audio/the tray/Wi-Fi power save all compile and link;
        it does not prove a real handshake or a real client connects - see
        README.md for exactly what is and is not verified.
